---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import countries from "../data/countries.json";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is Purchasing Power Parity (PPP) in global economics?",
    a: "Purchasing Power Parity (PPP) is a foundational macroeconomic metric that measures absolute currency capabilities by evaluating how many currency units are required to buy an identical basket of consumer goods and services across different sovereign nations, correcting the visual distortions caused by spot market exchange rates.",
  },
  {
    q: "How does the RealSalaryCheck PPP Calculator compute my financial verdict?",
    a: "RealSalaryCheck doesn't perform linear market currency multiplication. Our engine fetches real-time fiat exchange rates and immediately processes them against localized purchasing power parity conversion factors. It scales your current regional gross income into a normalized USD benchmark, calculates the lifestyle footprint multiplier for the destination country, and outputs your actual percentage change in purchasing power parity.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where does this calculator fetch its live economic indicator data?",
    a: "Our core calculation architectural baseline regularly synchronizes with global tracking databases, utilizing authentic purchasing power parity (PPP) conversion factors from the World Bank. For raw currency exchange transactions, our pipeline queries live, authoritative interbank foreign exchange feeds to ensure financial analysis accuracy at any given second.",
  },
  {
    q: "How should I read the final Net lifestyle value shift results?",
    a: "Our calculator returns three distinct verdicts: An 'Accept' badge means your purchasing power increases by over 15%, mathematically giving you a lifestyle upgrade. A 'Negotiate' badge signals a marginal shift between -5% and +15%, meaning your standard of living remains relatively similar. A 'Reject' badge warns that high destination prices will contract your disposable income velocity, leading to a financial lifestyle downgrade.",
  },

  {
    q: "What is a PPP Salary Calculator and why is it critical for tech talent?",
    a: "A PPP Salary Calculator is an international valuation tool that cross-references nominal cross-border job compensation packages against sovereign cost-of-living indices. For digital nomads and engineers, it eliminates numerical bias, showcasing exactly how far an overseas salary will go when spent inside the local economy.",
  },
  {
    q: "How does a standard Purchasing Power Parity Calculator work behind the scenes?",
    a: "A PPP calculator works by extracting a mathematical ratio based on national price level determinants. It divides the domestic cost of an indexed index basket by the target country's pricing for that same basket, calculating a baseline conversion factor that acts as a realistic cost of living comparison standard.",
  },
  {
    q: "Why is PPP better than standard foreign exchange (Forex) rates for salary comparison?",
    a: "Standard foreign exchange rates only dictate currency conversion values at a bank desk, reflecting volatile market speculations and trade balances. PPP reflects actual buying power and local living costs, providing a realistic assessment of financial leverage and asset building capability inside the target country.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I reliably compare international job offers using a PPP indexing matrix?",
    a: "Yes, you can. Utilizing a PPP index is the most accurate framework to evaluate international job offers because it estimates whether an overseas corporate package expands or contracts your lifestyle velocity, helping you identify if a higher numeric paycheck is hidden beneath an expensive relocation hub penalty.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does a PPP calculator directly account for local cost of living dynamics?",
    a: "Yes, PPP indicators are structurally intertwined with cost-of-living indexes. By continuously monitoring consumer basket fluctuations, a PPP calculator accurately captures price differences across daily staples, utility tariffs, public infrastructure, and localized service sectors.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is Purchasing Power Parity (PPP) exactly the same as the local cost of living?",
    a: "No, they are distinct concepts. PPP measures relative macroeconomic purchasing power differentials between sovereign national currencies as a whole, whereas the cost of living represents the granular, real-time monetary expenditure required to maintain a specific standard of living within a defined municipal perimeter or city tier.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can PPP metrics be used to negotiate remote job salary distributions?",
    a: "Absolutely. Remote workers, freelancers, and distributed engineering assets routinely utilize PPP-adjusted salary models to benchmark their compensation. This ensures fair, location-agnostic corporate packages when working for high-capital tech zones like Silicon Valley or London from lower-cost regions.",
  },
  {
    q: "How accurate is a World Bank-based PPP Salary Calculator?",
    a: "PPP calculators provide highly reliable, institutional-grade estimates for baseline national comparisons because they rely on extensive macroeconomic price updates. However, users should treat it as a foundational benchmark, as individual household spending habits, specialized dietary needs, and local city premiums introduce personal variables.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does the standard PPP calculation account for personal income tax brackets?",
    a: "No, classic purchasing power parity conversion models do not incorporate sovereign income tax laws or local state deductions. Because cross-border fiscal frameworks vary significantly based on individual investments and marital status, tax adjustments must always be calculated separately.",
  },
  {
    q: "Should I compare international compensation using pre-tax or post-tax salaries?",
    a: "For an absolute reality check, post-tax (net take-home) salaries provide the most realistic comparison. Evaluating post-tax income ensures that you are factoring in the destination country's fiscal obligations, revealing your true liquid cash velocity for discretionary spending and active savings.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can a PPP analysis effectively guide cross-border relocation decisions?",
    a: "Yes, a comprehensive PPP analysis is a critical data point for any cross-border relocation strategy. It strips away numerical illusions, helping you clearly visualize whether moving to a foreign market will upscale your standard of living, preserve your current economic status, or impose an unwanted financial compromise.",
  },
  {
    q: "Why do PPP-adjusted salaries differ so drastically from exchange-rate conversions?",
    a: "They diverge because exchange-rate conversions operate under the assumption that a dollar has the same purchasing capacity everywhere, which is false. PPP-adjusted metrics recognize that lower-income economies often feature much lower price levels for non-traded local services, drastically increasing your domestic buying power.",
  },
  {
    q: "What primary global data infrastructure is used in this calculator?",
    a: "This calculator utilizes the official Purchasing Power Parity conversion factors continuously updated and maintained by the World Bank's International Comparison Program (ICP), paired with real-time operational interbank fiat spot indicators.",
  },
  {
    q: "Who stands to benefit the most from utilizing a PPP Salary Calculator?",
    a: "This tool provides critical financial clarity for international job seekers evaluating corporate relocation offers, global remote workers auditing remote parity benchmarks, corporate HR departments planning global mobility budgets, and expats managing cross-border financial transitions.",
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Real Salary Check | Global Tech PPP Calculator & Cost of Living Index"
  description="Calculate your true purchasing power parity (PPP) and evaluate international job offers accurately across 35+ countries based on World Bank Indices."
>
  <main
    class="w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-6 pt-6 md:pt-10 pb-20 overflow-hidden"
  >
    <div class="text-center mb-8 md:mb-10 animate-fade-in">
      <div
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 mb-4 rounded-full border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-600 light-mode:text-emerald-700 text-[10px] font-bold tracking-widest uppercase"
      >
        <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
          <path
            fill-rule="evenodd"
            d="M16.707 5.293a1 1 0 010 1.414l-8 8a1 1 0 01-1.414 0l-4-4a1 1 0 011.414-1.414L8 12.586l7.293-7.293a1 1 0 011.414 0z"
            clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
        </svg>
        World Bank Indices & Live Rates
      </div>
      <h1
        class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight mb-4"
        style="color: var(--logo-primary)"
      >
        RealSalaryCheck
      </h1>
      <p
        class="text-sm md:text-base max-w-xl mx-auto font-medium leading-relaxed"
        style="color: var(--nav-text)"
      >
        Evaluate international job offers accurately with our advanced <strong
          >PPP salary calculator</strong
        >. Discover your true <strong>purchasing power parity (PPP)</strong> and get
        an instant <strong>cost of living comparison</strong> before you relocate.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div
      class="rounded-2xl p-4 md:p-6 space-y-4 transition-all duration-500 shadow-xl hover:shadow-2xl animate-fade-in-delay-1"
      style="background-color: var(--card-bg); border: 1px solid var(--card-border);"
    >
      <div
        class="p-3 md:p-4 rounded-xl border w-full text-left transition-colors duration-300 hover:border-zinc-500/40"
        style="background-color: var(--inner-box); border-color: var(--card-border);"
      >
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div class="w-full">
            <label
              class="block text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1.5 opacity-80"
              style="color: var(--nav-text)">Current Country</label
            >
            <div class="relative group w-full">
              <select
                id="currentCountry"
                class="w-full appearance-none rounded-xl px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold focus:outline-none transition-all cursor-pointer hover:bg-white/5"
                style="background-color: var(--input-bg); border: 1px solid var(--input-border); color: var(--input-text);"
              >
                {
                  countries
                    .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))
                    .map((c) => (
                      <option value={c.code} selected={c.code === "IN"}>
                        {c.name} ({c.currency})
                      </option>
                    ))
                }
              </select>
              <div
                class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 right-4 flex items-center transition-transform group-hover:translate-y-0.5"
                style="color: var(--nav-text)"
              >
                <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none">
                  <path
                    d="M2 4L6 8L10 4"
                    stroke="currentColor"
                    stroke-width="2.5"
                    stroke-linecap="round"
                    stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
                </svg>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <label
              class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider opacity-70"
              style="color: var(--nav-text);">Current Gross Salary / YR</label
            >
            <div class="relative">
              <div
                class="absolute inset-y-0 left-0 w-14 flex items-center justify-center pointer-events-none"
              >
                <span
                  id="currentSymbol"
                  class="text-sm font-bold opacity-70"
                  style="color: var(--text-secondary);">$</span
                >
              </div>
              <input
                type="number"
                id="currentSalary"
                placeholder="e.g. 100000"
                class="w-full rounded-xl pl-11 pr-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-emerald-500/40"
                style="background-color: var(--input-bg); border: 1px solid var(--input-border); color: var(--input-text);"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        class="p-3 md:p-4 rounded-xl border w-full text-left transition-colors duration-300 hover:border-zinc-500/40"
        style="background-color: var(--inner-box); border-color: var(--card-border);"
      >
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div class="w-full">
            <label
              class="block text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1.5 opacity-80"
              style="color: var(--nav-text)">Offer Country</label
            >
            <div class="relative group w-full">
              <select
                id="offerCountry"
                class="w-full appearance-none rounded-xl px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold focus:outline-none transition-all cursor-pointer hover:bg-white/5"
                style="background-color: var(--input-bg); border: 1px solid var(--input-border); color: var(--input-text);"
              >
                {
                  countries
                    .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))
                    .map((c) => (
                      <option value={c.code} selected={c.code === "US"}>
                        {c.name} ({c.currency})
                      </option>
                    ))
                }
              </select>
              <div
                class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 right-4 flex items-center transition-transform group-hover:translate-y-0.5"
                style="color: var(--nav-text)"
              >
                <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none">
                  <path
                    d="M2 4L6 8L10 4"
                    stroke="currentColor"
                    stroke-width="2.5"
                    stroke-linecap="round"
                    stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
                </svg>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <label
              class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider opacity-70"
              style="color: var(--nav-text);">Offered Gross Salary / YR</label
            >
            <div class="relative">
              <div
                class="absolute inset-y-0 left-0 w-14 flex items-center justify-center pointer-events-none"
              >
                <span
                  id="offerSymbol"
                  class="text-sm font-bold opacity-70"
                  style="color: var(--text-secondary);">$</span
                >
              </div>
              <input
                type="number"
                id="offerSalary"
                placeholder="e.g. 80000"
                class="w-full rounded-xl pl-11 pr-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-emerald-500/40"
                style="background-color: var(--input-bg); border: 1px solid var(--input-border); color: var(--input-text);"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <button
        id="calcBtn"
        tabindex="3"
        class="w-full rounded-xl py-3.5 text-sm font-black tracking-widest uppercase transition-all duration-300 shadow-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-center items-center hover:opacity-90 active:scale-[0.98]"
        style="background-color: var(--logo-primary); color: var(--bg-main);"
      >
        <span>COMPARE INTERNATIONAL SALARY NOW →</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div
      id="result"
      class="hidden mt-10 space-y-4 scroll-mt-24 transition-all duration-500"
    >
      <div
        id="verdictBanner"
        class="rounded-2xl p-5 border text-center shadow-lg"
        style="background-color: var(--card-bg); border-color: var(--card-border);"
      >
        <span
          id="verdictBadge"
          class="text-[11px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest px-5 py-2 rounded-full border"
        ></span>
      </div>

      <div
        class="rounded-2xl p-5 md:p-6 border shadow-lg"
        style="background-color: var(--card-bg); border-color: var(--card-border);"
      >
        <h2
          class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-4 flex items-center gap-2"
          style="color: var(--text-primary);"
        >
          <svg
            class="w-4 h-4 text-emerald-500"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
          >
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              stroke-width="2"
              d="M3 6l3 1m0 0l-3 9a5.002 5.002 0 006.001 0M6 7l3 9M6 7l6-2m6 2l3-1m-3 1l-3 9a5.002 5.002 0 006.001 0M18 7l3 9m-3-9l-6-2m0-2v2m0 16V5m0 16H9m3 0h3"
            ></path>
          </svg>
          Lifestyle Value (PPP Adjusted)
        </h2>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
          <div
            class="rounded-xl p-4 border text-center"
            style="background-color: var(--inner-box); border-color: var(--card-border);"
          >
            <p
              class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 opacity-70"
              style="color: var(--nav-text);"
            >
              Current Life Value
            </p>
            <p
              id="pppCurrent"
              class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black"
              style="color: var(--logo-primary);"
            >
            </p>
          </div>
          <div
            class="rounded-xl p-4 border text-center"
            style="background-color: var(--inner-box); border-color: var(--card-border);"
          >
            <p
              class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 opacity-70"
              style="color: var(--nav-text);"
            >
              Offered Life Value
            </p>
            <p
              id="pppOffer"
              class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black"
              style="color: var(--logo-primary);"
            >
            </p>
          </div>
          <div
            class="col-span-2 md:col-span-1 rounded-xl p-4 border text-center relative overflow-hidden"
            style="background-color: var(--inner-box); border-color: var(--card-border);"
          >
            <p
              class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 opacity-70"
              style="color: var(--nav-text);"
            >
              Purchasing Power Shift
            </p>
            <p id="pppChange" class="text-2xl font-black"></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        class="rounded-2xl p-5 md:p-6 border bg-amber-500/5"
        style="border-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.2);"
      >
        <h3
          class="text-sm font-bold mb-3 text-amber-500 flex items-center gap-2"
        >
          <svg
            class="w-5 h-5"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
          >
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              stroke-width="2"
              d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"
            ></path>
          </svg>
          Reality Check: What does this mean?
        </h3>
        <p
          id="dynamicExplanation"
          class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4"
          style="color: var(--text-secondary);"
        >
        </p>

        <div class="border-t border-amber-500/10 pt-4 mt-4">
          <p
            class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 text-amber-500/80"
          >
            ⚠️ Crucial Manual Considerations:
          </p>
          <ul class="text-xs space-y-2" style="color: var(--nav-text);">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-500">•</span>
              <b>Income Taxes:</b> This calculation is based on GROSS income. You
              must calculate the income tax of your destination country manually,
              as it varies by marital status and state.
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-500">•</span>
              <b>City Tier Premiums:</b> PPP is a national average. If moving to an
              expensive tech hub (e.g., London, NYC, San Francisco), housing costs
              will heavily skew this number downwards.
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-500">•</span>
              <b>Healthcare & Education:</b> Factor in private insurance costs or
              schooling fees if they are not publicly subsidized in your target country.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <button
        id="showCalcBtn"
        class="w-full rounded-xl py-3 text-sm font-bold border transition-all duration-200 cursor-pointer hover:bg-white/5"
        style="border-color: var(--card-border); color: var(--nav-text);"
      >
        Show Calculation Breakdown ↓
      </button>

      <div
        id="calcBreakdown"
        class="hidden rounded-2xl p-5 md:p-6 border space-y-4 shadow-lg"
        style="background-color: var(--card-bg); border-color: var(--card-border);"
      >
        <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-2">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold" style="color: var(--text-primary);">
            Mathematical Breakdown:
          </p>
          <button
            id="copyBreakdownBtn"
            class="text-xs font-bold tracking-wider uppercase border rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 transition-all duration-200 active:scale-95 cursor-pointer flex items-center gap-1.5 hover:bg-white/5"
            style="border-color: var(--card-border); background-color: var(--inner-box); color: var(--nav-text);"
          >
            <svg
              class="w-3.5 h-3.5"
              fill="none"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="2.5"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                d="M8 5H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-1M8 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M8 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2m0 0h2a2 2 0 012 2v3m2 4H10m0 0l3-3m-3 3l3 3"
              ></path>
            </svg>
            <span id="copyBtnText">Copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div
          id="breakdownContent"
          class="space-y-3 text-xs md:text-sm font-mono leading-relaxed p-4 rounded-xl border"
          style="background-color: var(--inner-box); border-color: var(--card-border); color: var(--nav-text);"
        >
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <div
    id="instantConverterWrapper"
    class="fixed bottom-4 right-4 md:bottom-6 md:right-6 z-40 font-sans text-left print:hidden"
  >
    <div
      id="converterTimedPop"
      class="absolute bottom-16 right-2 text-[10px] font-black tracking-widest uppercase px-4 py-2 rounded-xl shadow-2xl backdrop-blur-md transition-all duration-500 ease-out translate-y-2 opacity-0 pointer-events-none border select-none"
      style="background-color: var(--card-bg); border-color: var(--card-border); color: var(--logo-primary);"
    >
      Currency Converter
    </div>

    <button
      id="converterTriggerBtn"
      class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shadow-2xl transition-all duration-300 active:scale-95 hover:scale-105 cursor-pointer border"
      style="background-color: var(--card-bg); border-color: var(--card-border); color: var(--logo-primary); display: flex;"
    >
      <svg
        class="w-5 h-5"
        fill="none"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2.5"
      >
        <path
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          d="M8 7h12m0 0l-4-4m4 4l-4 4m0 6H4m0 0l4 4m-4-4l4-4"></path>
      </svg>
    </button>

    <div
      id="converterExpandedPanel"
      class="hidden w-72 sm:w-80 md:w-96 rounded-2xl shadow-2xl border p-3.5 backdrop-blur-xl transition-all duration-300 transform scale-95 opacity-0 origin-bottom-right"
      style="background-color: var(--card-bg); border-color: var(--card-border);"
    >
      <div
        class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2.5 border-b pb-1.5"
        style="border-color: var(--card-border);"
      >
        <h3
          class="text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest flex items-center gap-1.5"
          style="color: var(--text-primary);"
        >
          <span
            class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 animate-pulse"
          ></span> Live Forex
        </h3>
        <button
          id="closeConverterBtn"
          class="text-xs font-bold opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-all cursor-pointer p-1"
          style="color: var(--nav-text);">✕</button
        >
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-2.5">
        <div
          class="p-2 rounded-xl border flex items-center justify-between gap-1.5 transition-colors focus-within:border-emerald-500/50"
          style="background-color: var(--inner-box); border-color: var(--card-border);"
        >
          <select
            id="instantSrcCountry"
            aria-label="Dynamic Forex Source Profile Dropdown"
            class="bg-transparent border-0 font-bold text-xs focus:outline-none focus:ring-0 cursor-pointer w-24 text-ellipsis overflow-hidden"
            style="color: var(--text-primary);"
          >
            {
              countries.map((c) => (
                <option
                  value={c.code}
                  style="background-color: var(--input-bg); color: var(--input-text);"
                >
                  {c.currency} ({c.symbol})
                </option>
              ))
            }
          </select>
          <input
            type="number"
            id="instantSrcAmount"
            placeholder="0.00"
            class="bg-transparent border-0 text-right font-black text-sm focus:outline-none focus:ring-0 w-full p-0"
            style="color: var(--logo-primary);"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="flex justify-center -my-2 relative z-10 select-none">
          <div
            class="text-[10px] p-0.5 rounded-full border shadow-sm font-black bg-zinc-800"
            style="background-color: var(--card-bg); border-color: var(--card-border); color: var(--nav-text);"
          >
            ⇅
          </div>
        </div>

        <div
          class="p-2 rounded-xl border flex items-center justify-between gap-1.5 transition-colors focus-within:border-emerald-500/50"
          style="background-color: var(--inner-box); border-color: var(--card-border);"
        >
          <select
            id="instantTargetCountry"
            aria-label="Dynamic Forex Target Profile Dropdown"
            class="bg-transparent border-0 font-bold text-xs focus:outline-none focus:ring-0 cursor-pointer w-24 text-ellipsis overflow-hidden"
            style="color: var(--text-primary);"
          >
            {
              countries.map((c) => (
                <option
                  value={c.code}
                  selected={c.code === "US"}
                  style="background-color: var(--input-bg); color: var(--input-text);"
                >
                  {c.currency} ({c.symbol})
                </option>
              ))
